## Software & Container Infrastructure

### Docker

Docker is used to run self-hosted applications in isolated containers, allowing services to be managed independently.

### Portainer

Portainer provides a web-based management interface for the Docker environment.

It is used to manage and inspect the containerised services running on the Raspberry Pi.

### Immich — Photo Management

Immich provides a self-hosted photo backup and management platform.

The service uses an externally connected M.2 SATA SSD for local photo storage.

**Key capabilities:**
- Self-hosted photo backup and management
- Containerised application deployment
- External storage integration
- Local control over stored photographs

### AdGuard Home — DNS Filtering

AdGuard Home provides DNS-based filtering for devices using the service.

Configured blocklists help filter advertising, tracking domains and known malicious domains.

**Key capabilities:**
- DNS query filtering
- Advertisement and tracker blocking
- Malware-domain blocklists
- Centralised DNS filtering configuration

## Network Architecture

The Raspberry Pi is connected to my home network using wired Ethernet.

The wider network infrastructure also includes a Vodafone THG3000 router repurposed into a wireless access point.

The access point was configured by disabling its DHCP server and setting up a wireless network named **Ayub's Office**.

This allows the spare router to provide wireless connectivity while avoiding conflicting DHCP services on the same network.

